# Python

- Format and lint with Ruff (`uv run ruff format .`, `uv run ruff check --fix .`).
- Prefer SQL dbt models for transforms; use Python only when necessary.
- Ingest scripts (`scripts/ingest_raw.py`): preserve source column names and types; only add technical metadata (`_source_file`, `_loaded_at`).
- dbt Python models must expose `def model(dbt, session):` and return a relation DuckDB can materialize.
- For pure Python helpers, use pytest-style TDD when adding logic.
